      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Divisible by 3 means the number must have digits that add up to a number that is divisble by 3. This eliminates the numbers 1, 2, and 3. This only leaves 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9. There are 3 numbers out of 6 which are composite numbers, or numbers that are divisible by 3. This means that there is 1 number that is divisible by 3 in half the numbers. In probability, half the cases is 1/2. 1/2 , or .5 is the result .\n\nThe answer is \\frac{1}{2}.",
